==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*lesaną}}. The sense “read” is derived from West Germanic (Old Saxon or Old High German), a semantic loan of {{noncog|la|legō|t=gather, read}}; for reading the Germanic [[rune]]s, which were in use before the adoption of the Latin alphabet, the usual verb had been {{m|non|ráða}} (same as {{cog|en|read}}).

===Verb===
{{non-verb}}

# to [[gather]], [[pick]]
# to [[read]]

